  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 8.3, the ANP representation of a simplified version of the same problem — the figure that shows what ANP adds to AHP. The green goal box (\"Goal: Rank m alternatives considering n criteria\") feeds three blue criteria boxes, and two peach alternative boxes sit below. Two things differ from Figure 8.1. Every edge now carries an arrowhead, so direction is asserted; and the criteria are joined to one another by dash-dot double-headed arrows — Criterion 1 to Criterion 2, Criterion 2 to Criterion 3, and Criterion 1 to Criterion 3 in an arc over the top — which is the interdependence AHP's hierarchy forbids. The alternatives also point back up into the criteria as well as receiving arrows from them, so the feedback runs both ways.",
